{"qid":"Q805","names":["Republic of Yemen"],"title":"Republic of Yemen","endonym":{"native":"الجمهوريّة اليمنية","lang":"ar"},"capsule":"The Republic of Yemen was created on 22 May 1990 by the unification of North Yemen (Yemen Arab Republic) and South Yemen (PDRY), with Sanaa as capital and Ali Abdullah Saleh as first president. It is a presidential republic that has since been wracked by civil conflict, including a 1994 war and the post-2014 war involving the Houthi movement. It is the internationally recognized successor sharing the seat of unified Yemen.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. This polity has not yet received individual source review: treat extents as indicative atlas convention.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[],"britannica":"place/Yemen","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Yemen","rulers":[{"qid":"Q483672","name":"Ali Abdullah Saleh","start":1990,"end":2012,"image":"Ali Abdullah Saleh - Putin meeting 2010-06-30 (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ali%20Abdullah%20Saleh%20-%20Putin%20meeting%202010-06-30%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 4.0","artist":"premier.gov.ru","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"علي عبد الله صالح","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q1322893","name":"Haidar Abu Bakr al-Attas","start":1990,"end":1994,"image":null,"nativeName":"حيدر أبو بكر العطاس","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q2622743","name":"Abdul Aziz Abdul Ghani","start":1994,"end":1997,"image":"Abdul Aziz Abdul Ghani (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Abdul%20Aziz%20Abdul%20Ghani%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicens